sweet fb: do not wait for a latch when nothing was handed to the MDP

0268 turns on the honest swap completion (fEarly/fSwapSync) for the scanout mode, but
when every scanout frame is declined the pipe is never programmed, fLastFlush stays 0 and
swapWaitInner spins until its 1.5-frame limit answering kIOReturnBusy. CoreAnimation then
stops submitting frames: on raphael that was 2810 swap_wait_timeouts and 35 swaps in 33
minutes, so the picture froze and touches had no visible effect. Nothing handed over means
nothing to latch, so answer done.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -2185,6 +2185,15 @@
 	if (swapReady(id)) {
 		return kIOReturnSuccess;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * 0269: nothing has been handed to the MDP yet (no flipSetup, or every scanout frame declined), so
+	 * there is no latch to wait for. Without this the honest swap completion added by 0268 waits on
+	 * fLastFlush == 0 until the 1.5-frame limit and answers kIOReturnBusy for ever: CoreAnimation then
+	 * stops submitting frames and the UI freezes (raphael: 2810 swap_wait_timeouts, 35 swaps in 33 min).
+	 */
+	if (fLastFlush == 0) {
+		return kIOReturnSuccess;
+	}
 	volatile uint32_t *flush = (volatile uint32_t *)(fMdp + SWEET_MDP_CTL0 + SWEET_MDP_CTL_FLUSH);
 	uint64_t t0 = mach_absolute_time(), limit;
 	bool sawBusy = false, kicked = false;
